of schemas, validation row IDs, and a smoke-test sample predictions file. The private directory receives only the validation labels keyed by PassengerId. I guard against leakage by never copying the full labeled source into public and by stripping Survived from the validation inputs. The sample predictions are derived deterministically from public data alone (constant 0) so they don\'t leak label information while still being valid for the evaluator smoke test. Split indices are recomputed the same way in evaluate.py to align by PassengerId.\n</explanation>\n<code>\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\n\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n\nSEED = 42\nTEST_SIZE = 0.2\n\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument("--input_dir", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument("--public_dir", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument("--private_dir", required=True)\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    input_dir = os.path.abspath(args.input_dir)\n    public_dir = os.path.abspath(args.public_dir)\n    private_dir = os.path.abspath(args.private_dir)\n\n    train_src = os.path.join(input_dir, "train_data", "train.csv")\n    test_src = os.path.join(input_dir, "predict_data", "test.csv")\n    for p in (train_src, test_src):\n        if not os.path.isfile(p):\n            sys.exit(f"[split] missing input file: {p}")\n\n    train = pd.read_csv(train_src)\n    test = pd.read_csv(test_src)\n\n    if "Survived" not in train.columns:\n        sys.exit("[split] train.csv missing \'Survived\'")\n    if "PassengerId" not in train.columns or "PassengerId" not in test.columns:\n        sys.exit("[split] PassengerId column required")\n\n    # Recover original order: train_test_split preserves input order within splits,\n    # so pass the original frame as-is.\n    idx = range(len(train))\n    y = train["Survived"].values\n\n    train_idx, val_idx = train_test_split(\n        list(idx),\n        test_size=TEST_SIZE,\n       